<ContentLayout title="Lumen Browser — Independent Web Browser in Development | Aurora" description="Lumen is the web browser workstream of the Aurora ecosystem. Its architecture, rendering engine, platforms and privacy behavior are not yet verified publicly." eyebrow="ECOSYSTEM / WEB BROWSER" heading="Lumen: the web browser of the Aurora ecosystem" lead="Lumen is the browser workstream of the Aurora ecosystem. It is in development; its rendering engine, supported platforms, compatibility and privacy behavior are not yet documented as verified product capabilities.">
  <section class="section shell content-columns">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">DEVELOPMENT STATUS</p><h2>In development</h2><p class="content-copy">Lumen is an active product workstream, not a released browser.</p><p class="eyebrow">PUBLIC EVIDENCE STATUS</p><h3>Not verified</h3><p class="content-copy">No browser implementation, compatibility matrix, performance benchmark or security assessment has been reviewed for this website update. No release or capability guarantee is made.</p></div>
    <div><p class="eyebrow">WHAT IS KNOWN</p><ul class="content-list"><li>Lumen is the browser workstream of the Aurora ecosystem.</li><li>It is intended to complement Aurora OS as a distinct application.</li><li>Its rendering engine and technical stack are not publicly verified here.</li><li>No supported-platform or compatibility guarantee is published.</li></ul></div>
  </section>
  <section class="section shell article-content">
    <h2>Product direction</h2>
    <p class="content-copy">Lumen is being developed as an independent browsing experience within the Aurora ecosystem. The available public information does not establish whether its rendering engine is custom-built or based on an existing project. That decision should be stated explicitly when it is confirmed, rather than inferred from the product's name or visual concepts.</p>
    <p class="content-copy">A browser is a security-sensitive application: it processes hostile remote content, manages credentials and sessions, and mediates access to local resources. Lumen's public documentation should make these responsibilities visible instead of relying on broad privacy or security claims.</p>
    <div class="principle-grid">
      <article class="principle-card"><span>01 / WEB PLATFORM</span><h3>Compatibility</h3><p>Document supported web standards, rendering behavior and known compatibility gaps against repeatable test suites.</p></article>
      <article class="principle-card"><span>02 / ISOLATION</span><h3>Content boundaries</h3><p>Explain how sites, tabs, processes and privileged browser components are separated. No isolation guarantee is claimed until implemented and tested.</p></article>
      <article class="principle-card"><span>03 / PRIVACY</span><h3>Data transparency</h3><p>Specify local storage, synchronization, telemetry, crash reporting and external services before describing the privacy model.</p></article>
      <article class="principle-card"><span>04 / EXTENSIBILITY</span><h3>Permission review</h3><p>Define extension permissions, provenance, update policy and compatibility checks before accepting third-party code.</p></article>
    </div>
    <h2>Privacy and engineering</h2>
    <p class="content-copy">No complete product privacy policy or browser security assessment has been verified for Lumen. Read the <a href="/en/engineering/privacy/">privacy documentation</a> for the questions that remain to be answered, and the <a href="/en/development/">development register</a> for the current evidence boundary.</p>
    <h2>What a credible browser release must publish</h2>
    <ul class="content-list"><li>Supported operating systems and minimum runtime requirements.</li><li>Rendering engine and web-platform compatibility information.</li><li>Process and site-isolation design, including known limitations.</li><li>Permission model, extension policy and update mechanism.</li><li>Privacy disclosures, security advisories and reproducible test results.</li></ul>
    <p class="evidence-note">This is a documentation and verification checklist. It does not assert that Lumen currently implements any listed capability.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="section shell product-destination">
    <div><p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> EXTEND THE BROWSER</p><h2>Lumen extensions</h2><p class="content-copy">A planned destination for extensions designed for Lumen. No extension packages, compatibility data or installation resources are currently published.</p></div>
    <a class="button button-primary" href="/en/ecosystem/browser/extensions/">Explore extensions <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a>
  </section>
</ContentLayout>